  <data name="Settings_ViewReleaseNotes" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Versionshinweise auf GitHub anzeigen</value>
    <comment>[button] Link inside the highlighted panel that appears when a newer version is available. Opens the release page in the browser. GitHub is never translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Warning_SignedUpdatesRecommended" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aus Sicherheitsgründen werden signierte Updates empfohlen.</value>
    <comment>[description] Warning shown on the "Updates &amp; Security" card on the Settings hub when the user has turned off the requirement that update installers carry a valid signature.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DiskMonitorStarting" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Datenträgerüberwachung startet</value>
    <comment>[status] Line in the 'Global status' box at the bottom of the navigation rail. Shown while the background free-space monitor is doing its first pass; replaced by Shell_DrivesHealthy or Shell_LowestFreeSpace afterwards. Narrow column, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DriveHealthWarningTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Laufwerkszustand erfordert Aufmerksamkeit</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the Windows tray balloon notification raised when a drive's SMART health reading turns Warning or Critical. The body is composed at runtime from the drive name and the provider's own message. This warns about hardware condition, not about disk space.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_DrivesHealthy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Laufwerke fehlerfrei</value>
    <comment>[status] Free-space summary shown in the navigation rail's 'Global status' box and in the top status strip when no drive is anywhere near full. 'Drives' means storage drives/volumes. This is the good-news counterpart of Shell_LowestFreeSpace.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_GlobalStatus" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Gesamtstatus</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LastScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Letzte Überprüfung: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the main window's top status strip. {0} is the root folder path of the most recent scan, for example C:\Users\Ada. The line is trimmed with an ellipsis when it does not fit, so keep the leading label short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LatestScanUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Letzte Überprüfung nicht verfügbar</value>
    <comment>[status] Line in the 'Global status' box at the bottom of the navigation rail. Shown before the most recent scan session has been loaded from the database; replaced once it is. Narrow column (about 270 px), so keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowDiskBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Auf {0} sind nur noch {1} % frei ({2} GB).</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Body of the low-disk-space tray notification. {0} is the drive name as Windows reports it (for example 'C:\'), {1} is the whole-number percentage of free space, {2} is the free space in gigabytes already formatted to one decimal place. Keep all three placeholders and do not renumber them.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowDiskTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wenig Speicherplatz</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the Windows tray balloon notification raised by the background monitor when a drive drops below the warning or critical free-space threshold. Body text is Shell_LowDiskBody. Windows truncates long notification titles.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_LowestFreeSpace" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Geringster freier Speicherplatz: {0}</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_MonitoringActive" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überwachung aktiv</value>
    <comment>[status] Status word in the main window's top status strip, far right. Means the background disk-space monitor is running. Replaced at runtime by Shell_DrivesHealthy or Shell_LowestFreeSpace once the monitor has taken its first reading. Very tight horizontal space - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_NoScanLoaded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keine Überprüfung geladen</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the main window's top status strip, right-aligned next to the product name. Shown before any scan result has been read from the database; replaced at runtime by Shell_LastScan once a scan exists. Very tight horizontal space - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_NoScansYet" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Noch keine Überprüfungen</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_ScanInProgress" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>wird ausgeführt</value>
    <comment>[status] Substituted for a completion timestamp in the navigation rail's status line when the most recent scan has not finished. It is appended after the scan status and a middle dot, so it reads like 'Running - in progress'. Lower-case on purpose: it is a sentence fragment, not a standalone label.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_StartScanHint" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung starten, um Daten für den Überprüfungsbereich zu erfassen</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Line in the navigation rail's 'Global status' box when the database holds no scan sessions at all. Tells a first-time user what to do to populate the app. 'Scan' is the noun/verb for indexing a folder tree; 'workspace data' means the indexed results the other pages read from.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Speicher-Kommandozentrale v2</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_Exit" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Beenden</value>
    <comment>[button] Last entry in the tray icon's right-click menu, below a separator. Quits the application entirely rather than hiding it back to the notification area. Use the same word Windows uses for quitting an app from a tray menu.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Benachrichtigungen zu wenig Speicherplatz sind für 12 Stunden angehalten.</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Body of the confirmation tray notification after the user pauses notifications. States the fixed pause length; the 12 hours is hard-coded, so it is safe to spell out in the translation.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Benachrichtigungen angehalten</value>
    <comment>[dialog] Title of the confirmation tray notification shown immediately after the user picks 'Pause Notifications' from the tray icon's right-click menu. Body is Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_Open" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>StorageMaster öffnen</value>
    <comment>[button] First entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Restores the main window when the app is minimised to the notification area. 'StorageMaster' is the product name and stays untranslated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_PauseNotifications" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Benachrichtigungen anhalten</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Suppresses low-disk and drive-health tray notifications for 12 hours. Confirmed afterwards by Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedTitle and Shell_Tray_NotificationsPausedBody.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_ReviewDuplicates" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplikate prüfen</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Duplicates page, where duplicate files found by a scan are listed for review. Nothing is deleted by choosing this.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_SmartClean" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Intelligente Bereinigung starten</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Smart Cleaner page - it deletes nothing by itself, the user still reviews and confirms there. 'Smart Clean' is this app's name for the guided cleanup feature and must match the wording used for Nav_SmartCleaner.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Shell_Tray_StartScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung starten</value>
    <comment>[button] Entry in the tray icon's right-click menu. Opens the main window on the Scan page so the user can start indexing a folder. It does not begin a scan on its own.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Analyse" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfen &amp; analysieren</value>
    <comment>[button] Primary button in the Smart Cleaner page header. Starts the read-only scan that looks for junk files; it deletes nothing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seite „Intelligente Bereinigung“</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the whole Smart Cleaner page (the page reached from the Clean &gt; Smart Cleaner navigation entry). Announced when the page gains focus.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Card_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Datenmüll mit einem Klick entfernen</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the introduction card on the Smart Cleaner page, next to the page's icon.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_AuditWarning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Warnung zum Prüfprotokoll: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, reporting that the restore record for a removed item could not be written. {0} is the underlying technical detail, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_CleanupError" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigungsfehler: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, for an error raised during the cleanup. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fehler- und Prüfprotokolldetails</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the card on the Smart Cleaner page that lists the individual paths that could not be processed and any audit-record warnings.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_FailureDetails_ScanWarning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfungswarnung — {0}: {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] One entry in the 'Failure and audit details' list on the Smart Cleaner page, for a path the scan could not inspect. {0} is the path, {1} the underlying technical reason, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Result_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigungsergebnis</value>
    <comment>[header] Title of the banner that appears on the Smart Cleaner page after a cleanup run. The banner's body is the run's status sentence.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_AwaitingConfirmation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Warten auf die Bestätigung der Bereinigung…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page while the confirmation dialog is open and the app is waiting for the user's answer.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancelledNothingRemoved" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung abgebrochen, bevor ein Pfad entfernt wurde. Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when the run was cancelled before anything was touched.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancelledPartial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung nach teilweiser Ausführung abgebrochen. {0} Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when a cleanup was cancelled after part of the work was already done. {0} is the whole sentence from Safety_Smart_Summary_RecycleBin or Safety_Smart_Summary_Permanent, so keep a sentence break on both sides of it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancellingCleanup" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung wird abgebrochen…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page between the user pressing Cancel and the running cleanup actually stopping.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CancellingScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung wird abgebrochen…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page between the user pressing Cancel and the running scan actually stopping.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Cleaning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung läuft…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page while the confirmed cleanup is running.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CleanupCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung abgebrochen. Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch, da sich der Dateizustand geändert haben kann.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after the user cancelled a cleanup that had already started. Part of the files may already be gone, so a fresh scan is required.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CleanupFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung fehlgeschlagen. Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch, da sich der Dateizustand geändert haben kann.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after a cleanup that threw an error. Part of the files may already be gone, so a fresh scan is required.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Completed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung abgeschlossen. {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page after a fully successful run. {0} is the whole sentence from Safety_Smart_Summary_RecycleBin or Safety_Smart_Summary_Permanent.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_CompletedWithAuditWarning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung abgeschlossen. {0} Warnung zum Prüfprotokoll wird unten angezeigt.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when the run succeeded but a restore record could not be written. {0} is the whole sentence from Safety_Smart_Summary_RecycleBin or Safety_Smart_Summary_Permanent; the warning it points at is listed in the 'Failure and audit details' card underneath.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Found" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} Kategorie(n) mit Datenmüll gefunden. Wählen Sie aus, was entfernt werden soll.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after a complete scan that found junk. {0} is the number of categories. The English uses 'category/categories' to cover singular and plural; use whatever form is natural in the target language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_FoundPartial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} Kategorie(n) mit Datenmüll gefunden, aber {1} Pfad(e) konnten nicht geprüft werden. Es werden nur bestätigte Dateien aufgeführt.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after a scan that found something but could not read every location. {0} is the number of categories found, {1} the number of unreadable paths. The English uses 'category/categories' and 'path(s)' to cover singular and plural; use whatever form is natural in the target language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Initial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Klicken Sie auf „Überprüfen &amp; analysieren“, um Datenmüll automatisch zu finden.</value>
    <comment>[status] First status line on the Smart Cleaner page, shown before the user has scanned. The quoted text is the label of the page's own 'Scan &amp; Analyse' button (key Smart_Analyse) and must match that translation exactly.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_NoJunk" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Gute Nachrichten — auf diesem PC wurde kein nennenswerter Datenmüll gefunden!</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page when a complete scan found nothing worth removing. Deliberately upbeat; keep the friendly tone.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_NothingRemoved" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Es wurde nichts entfernt. {0} Pfad(e) sind fehlgeschlagen oder wurden übersprungen. Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when the run finished but removed nothing. {0} is the number of paths that failed or were skipped.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_PartiallyCompleted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bereinigung teilweise abgeschlossen. {0} {1} Pfad(e) sind fehlgeschlagen oder wurden übersprungen. Führen Sie vor einem erneuten Versuch eine neue Überprüfung durch.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line and result banner on the Smart Cleaner page when some paths could not be processed. {0} is the whole sentence from Safety_Smart_Summary_RecycleBin or Safety_Smart_Summary_Permanent; {1} is the number of failed or skipped paths.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_ScanCancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung abgebrochen.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page after the user cancelled the scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_ScanFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung fehlgeschlagen: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page when the scan threw an error. {0} is the underlying technical error text, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_ScanIncomplete" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung unvollständig: {0} Pfad(e) konnten nicht geprüft werden, und es wurden keine entfernbaren Dateien bestätigt.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page when the scan could not read some locations and found nothing it is sure about. {0} is the number of unreadable paths.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Status_Scanning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ihr PC wird nach Datenmüll durchsucht…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line on the Smart Cleaner page while the read-only scan is running.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüft sieben häufige Quellen von Datenmüll und entfernt nur, was Sie auswählen.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line description under the Smart Cleaner page title. 'Seven' is the fixed number of junk sources the scan looks at.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Intelligente Bereinigung</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading at the top of the Smart Cleaner page. Same words as the Nav_SmartCleaner navigation entry but rendered as the page's own large title; keep the two consistent.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Smart_TotalSelected_Label" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Insgesamt zur Bereinigung ausgewählt</value>
    <comment>[label] Small label above the combined size of the ticked junk categories, in the bar above the results list on the Smart Cleaner page. The value below it is a size such as '1.2 GB'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_CopyPath" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pfad kopieren</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the selection panel, and the same entry in the treemap's right-click menu: copies the full path of the selected item to the clipboard.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_DrillIntoFolder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In den Ordner wechseln</value>
    <comment>[button] First entry in the right-click menu on a treemap block, shown only for folders: redraws the map with that folder as the new root, one level deeper.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_OpenInResults" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In „Ergebnisse“ öffnen</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the selection panel that opens the Results page for the scan currently shown in the treemap. 'Results' is the name of another page in the app.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_RevealInExplorer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Im Explorer anzeigen</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the selection panel, and the same entry in the treemap's right-click menu: opens File Explorer with the selected file or folder shown. Explorer is the Windows file manager and keeps its Windows name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_SendToCleanup" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zur Prüfung an „Bereinigung“ senden</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the selection panel, and the same entry in the treemap's right-click menu: opens the Cleanup page for this scan so the user can review candidates there. It does not delete anything by itself. 'Cleanup' is the name of another page in the app.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Action_SendToDuplicate" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zur Prüfung an „Duplikate“ senden</value>
    <comment>[button] Button in the selection panel, and the same entry in the treemap's right-click menu: opens the Duplicates page for this scan so the user can review duplicate files there. It does not delete anything by itself. 'Duplicates' is the name of another page in the app.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_ComparingAgainst" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Vergleich mit der Überprüfung vom {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line inside the scan-delta card naming the older scan the current one is compared with. {0} is an already-formatted short date and time such as 18/08/2026 21:40.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_GrowingFolders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Gewachsene Ordner</value>
    <comment>[label] Label above the first of three lists in the scan-delta card: folders that take up more space than they did in the previous scan. Each row shows a path and the size increase.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfungsvergleich</value>
    <comment>[header] Section heading of the card below the treemap that compares this scan with the previous scan of the same root folder. 'Delta' means the difference between the two scans.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_NeedsTwoScans" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Für den Überprüfungsvergleich sind zwei abgeschlossene Überprüfungen mit demselben Startpfad erforderlich.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line inside the scan-delta card explaining why it is empty: a comparison needs two finished scans that started from the same root folder. Shown before a scan is chosen and whenever the map is reset.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_NewLargeFiles" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Neue große Dateien</value>
    <comment>[label] Label above the second of three lists in the scan-delta card: large files that exist now but did not exist in the previous scan. Each row shows a path and the file's size.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_NoPreviousScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Es wurde keine frühere abgeschlossene Überprüfung mit diesem Startpfad gefunden.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line inside the scan-delta card when the selected scan is the first one ever run for that root folder, so there is nothing to compare it against.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Delta_RemovedFiles" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Entfernte Dateien</value>
    <comment>[label] Label above the third of three lists in the scan-delta card: files that existed in the previous scan and are gone now. This is a report of what changed on disk, not a delete action. Each row shows a path and the size the file used to have.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_CopyPath" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Pfad konnte nicht kopiert werden: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when copying the selected item's path to the clipboard failed. {0} is the technical error text and stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_FolderLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Ordner konnte nicht geladen werden</value>
    <comment>[status] Start of a Space Map status line reporting that opening a folder from the treemap failed. Shown as this text, then a colon, then the technical error, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_FolderReload" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Ordner konnte nicht neu geladen werden</value>
    <comment>[status] Start of a Space Map status line reporting that redrawing the current folder after a filter change failed. Shown as this text, then a colon, then the technical error, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_OpenExplorer" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Datei-Explorer konnte nicht geöffnet werden: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the 'Reveal in Explorer' action could not start File Explorer. {0} is the technical error text and stays English. File Explorer keeps its Windows name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_ParentFolderLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der übergeordnete Ordner konnte nicht geladen werden</value>
    <comment>[status] Start of a Space Map status line reporting that going one level up with the 'Up' button failed. Shown as this text, then a colon, then the technical error, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_ReloadFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die Speicherbelegung konnte nicht neu geladen werden: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when an automatic refresh of the map failed. {0} is the technical error text and stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_SelectedScanLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die ausgewählte Überprüfung konnte nicht geladen werden</value>
    <comment>[status] Start of a Space Map status line reporting that loading the scan the user picked from the drop-down failed. Shown as this text, then a colon, then the technical error, which stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_SessionDataLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die Sitzungsdaten konnten nicht geladen werden.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the scan chosen while opening the page could not be read at all. A short message with no technical detail.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Error_SessionLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die Überprüfungen für die Speicherbelegung konnten nicht geladen werden</value>
    <comment>[status] Start of a Space Map status line reporting that loading the list of scans failed. Shown as this text, then a colon, then the technical error from Windows, which stays English. Write it so it reads correctly followed by ': &lt;error text&gt;'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_ExportPng_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Speicherbelegung als PNG exportieren</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of the button labelled 'PNG', which saves a screenshot of the treemap as a PNG image file. PNG stays PNG.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_CsvFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der CSV-Export ist fehlgeschlagen: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when writing the CSV report failed. {0} is the technical error text and stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_CsvSucceeded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der CSV-Bericht wurde nach {0} exportiert.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar confirming the table of the current folder's items was saved as a CSV file. {0} is the full file path. CSV stays CSV.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_HtmlFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der HTML-Export ist fehlgeschlagen: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when writing the HTML report failed. {0} is the technical error text and stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_HtmlSucceeded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der HTML-Bericht wurde nach {0} exportiert.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar confirming the table of the current folder's items was saved as an HTML page. {0} is the full file path. HTML stays HTML.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_NothingToExport" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Es gibt nichts zu exportieren. Laden Sie zuerst einen Ordner aus einer Überprüfung.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the user presses the PNG export button while the treemap is empty.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_PngFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der PNG-Export ist fehlgeschlagen: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when saving the treemap image failed. {0} is the technical error text from Windows and stays English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Export_PngSucceeded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der PNG-Screenshot wurde nach {0} exportiert.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar confirming the treemap image was saved. {0} is the full file path of the saved PNG file.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Filter_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dateien</value>
    <comment>[button] Filter button above the treemap that limits the map to files only. Sits next to 'Folders + files' and 'Folders' in one narrow row.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Filter_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordner</value>
    <comment>[button] Filter button above the treemap that limits the map to folders only. Sits next to 'Folders + files' and 'Files' in one narrow row.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Filter_FoldersAndFiles" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordner + Dateien</value>
    <comment>[button] First of three small filter buttons above the treemap. Selecting it shows both folders and files in the map. The other two are 'Folders' and 'Files'. Keep it short, the buttons sit side by side in one narrow row.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_GoUp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nach oben</value>
    <comment>[button] Small button above the treemap that navigates one folder level up, towards the scan root. Single word on a narrow pill button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Legend_Archives" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Archive</value>
    <comment>[label] Colour-key entry next to a small coloured square in the treemap legend: tiles in this colour are archive files such as ZIP or 7z.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Legend_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordner</value>
    <comment>[label] Colour-key entry next to a small coloured square in the treemap legend: tiles in this colour are folders. A legend entry, not a control.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Legend_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Legende</value>
    <comment>[label] Small heading above the colour key at the bottom of the selection panel, explaining what the treemap tile colours mean.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Legend_Images" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bilder</value>
    <comment>[label] Colour-key entry next to a small coloured square in the treemap legend: tiles in this colour are image files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Legend_Videos" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Videos</value>
    <comment>[label] Colour-key entry next to a small coloured square in the treemap legend: tiles in this colour are video files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_MinSize_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Filter für die Mindestgröße in Megabyte</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of that minimum-size spin box. Not visible on screen, so it may be longer than the visible header.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_MinSize_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Min. Größe MB</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above a small numeric spin box that hides everything smaller than the given number of megabytes from the treemap. The field is about 180 px wide, so the label must stay very short; MB is the unit symbol and stays MB.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Page_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seite „Speicherbelegung“</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of the whole Space Map page. Announced when the page gets focus; it is not visible on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_ScanSelector_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Auswahl der Überprüfung für die Speicherbelegung</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of that same scan drop-down on the Space Map page. Not visible on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_ScanSelector_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that picks which completed scan the treemap is drawn from. Scan here is the noun (a finished scan run), not a command.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Auswahl</value>
    <comment>[header] Section heading of the narrow panel to the right of the treemap, which describes the block the user last clicked.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_NoFolder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kein Ordner ausgewählt</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Placeholder shown in place of the current folder path above the treemap breadcrumbs, before any scan folder has been opened.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_NoItem" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kein Element ausgewählt</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Placeholder shown in the selection panel where the selected item's name would be, while nothing in the treemap is selected.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_NoPath" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wählen Sie einen Block in der Treemap aus.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Placeholder shown in the selection panel where the selected item's full path would be, while nothing is selected. Tells the user to click a rectangle in the map.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_PercentOfParent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} % des übergeordneten Ordners</value>
    <comment>[label] Value under the 'Share' label in the selection panel: how much of its containing folder the selected item takes up. {0} is an already-formatted number such as 12.4.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_Share" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Anteil</value>
    <comment>[label] Small label above the selected block's share of its parent folder, shown as a percentage, in the selection panel. Sits next to 'Size'. Share here means proportion, not sharing a file.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Selection_Size" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Größe</value>
    <comment>[label] Small label above the size in bytes of the selected treemap block, in the selection panel. Sits next to 'Share' in a two-column pair.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_LoadingChildren" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordnerinhalt wird geladen...</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar while the items inside the current folder are being read, before the treemap is redrawn.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_LoadingScans" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Abgeschlossene Überprüfungen werden geladen...</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar while the list of finished scans is being read from the database.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_LoadingSelectedScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die ausgewählte Überprüfung wird geladen...</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar right after the user picks a different scan from the drop-down, while its data is being loaded.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_NoChildrenMatchFilters" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keine Elemente entsprechen den aktuellen Filtern.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the current folder does contain items, but none pass the folder/file filter and the minimum-size filter, so the map is empty.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_NoCompletedScans" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Es sind keine abgeschlossenen Überprüfungen verfügbar.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the database holds no finished scan at all, so nothing can be mapped yet.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_PathCopied" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Pfad wurde in die Zwischenablage kopiert.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar confirming that the selected item's full path was copied to the clipboard.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_RequestedScanUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die angeforderte abgeschlossene Überprüfung ist nicht verfügbar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line in the Space Map information bar when the page was opened for one specific scan (from another page) and that scan is no longer in the database.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_SelectScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wählen Sie eine abgeschlossene Überprüfung aus, um die Speicherbelegung darzustellen.</value>
    <comment>[status] First status line shown in the Space Map information bar when the page opens and no scan has been chosen yet.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Status_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Status der Speicherbelegung</value>
    <comment>[title] Title of the information bar under the treemap. Its message body is the page's live status line, which is a separate string.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Interaktive Treemap, Überprüfungsvergleich und Aktionen mit vorgeschalteter Prüfung.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the Space Map page title, summarising what the page offers: a clickable treemap, a comparison against the previous scan, and actions that always route through a review step before anything is deleted.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Speicherbelegung</value>
    <comment>[title] Title at the top of the Space Map page. The page shows a treemap of how disk space is used by folders and files.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SpaceMap_Treemap_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Interaktive Treemap der Speicherbelegung</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of the treemap canvas itself: the large chart of nested rectangles, one per folder or file, sized by how much disk space each uses. Not visible on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Column_Category" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kategorie</value>
    <comment>[header] Column header over the file-category column in the file-type table on the Scan Workspace Overview tab.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Column_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dateien</value>
    <comment>[header] Column header over the file-count column in the file-type table on the Scan Workspace Overview tab. Plural noun meaning 'number of files'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Column_Size" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Größe</value>
    <comment>[header] Column header over the size column in the file-type table on the Scan Workspace Overview tab: the combined size of that category.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Delta_Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Details zum Überprüfungsvergleich finden Sie weiterhin unter „Speicherbelegung“, sofern vergleichbare Überprüfungen denselben Startpfad haben.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanatory text on the Delta tab of the Scan Workspace. Says the comparison between two scans is shown on the Space Map page instead, and only for scans that started from the same folder ('root').</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Delta_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfungsvergleich</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the placeholder on the Delta tab of the Scan Workspace. 'Delta' means the difference between two scans of the same folder.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_Action" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplikate prüfen</value>
    <comment>[button] Button on the Duplicates tab of the Scan Workspace that opens the duplicates page for this scan. Imperative.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_None" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Noch keine Duplikatanalyse ausgeführt.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Shown on the Scan Workspace, in the review-queue card and on the Duplicates tab, when duplicate detection has never been run for this scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_Summary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} Gruppen · {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] Summary of the latest duplicate detection run, shown in the Scan Workspace review-queue card and on the Duplicates tab. {0} is the number of duplicate groups found, pre-formatted with thousands separators; a group is one set of identical files. {1} is the run's state (an internal English word such as Completed). The separator is a middle dot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Duplicates_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplikatprüfung</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the placeholder on the Duplicates tab of the Scan Workspace, above a button that opens the duplicates page. Means the step where the user goes through duplicate files and decides which copies to keep.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Errors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fehler</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many paths the scanner could not read. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dateien</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many files the scan found. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordner</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of a readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is how many folders the scan found. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Metric_ScannedSize" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfte Größe</value>
    <comment>[label] Label of the first readout card on the Scan Workspace page. The value below is the combined size of everything this scan covered.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Overview_Composition" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zusammensetzung nach Dateityp</value>
    <comment>[header] Heading of the card on the Scan Workspace Overview tab that breaks the scan down by file category, showing how much of the scanned data each category accounts for.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Overview_ReviewQueue" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Prüfliste</value>
    <comment>[header] Heading of the card on the Scan Workspace Overview tab that summarises what is waiting for the user's review: duplicate findings and how much space could be recovered.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Page_AutomationName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Seite „Überprüfungsbereich“</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name for the whole Scan Workspace page, announced when it is opened. Not visible on screen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_Idle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Führen Sie eine Bereinigung oder eine Duplikatprüfung aus, um die Einsparungen zu schätzen.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card before anything has been analysed. Tells the user which two actions produce an estimate of how much space could be freed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_NoRun" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Führen Sie eine Duplikatprüfung aus, um den freigebbaren Speicherplatz zu schätzen.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card when the scan loaded but no duplicate run exists for it yet.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Reclaimable_Summary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} freigebbar aus der letzten Duplikatanalyse.</value>
    <comment>[status] Helper line in the Scan Workspace review-queue card. {0} is a data size, already formatted (for example '2.3 GB'), that could be freed by removing redundant copies found in the most recent duplicate run. Nothing is deleted by this text.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Action" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Speicherbelegung öffnen</value>
    <comment>[button] Button on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace that navigates to the Space Map page for this scan. Same English text as the heading above it, but this one is the button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die interaktive Treemap wird mit dem Kontext dieser Überprüfung geöffnet, und Aktionen, die Daten löschen, laufen weiterhin über die Prüfabläufe.</value>
    <comment>[description] Explanatory text on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace. Says that opening the Space Map carries this scan's data over, and that anything which deletes files there still goes through a review step first rather than acting immediately.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_SpaceMap_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Speicherbelegung öffnen</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the placeholder shown on the Space Map tab of the Scan Workspace, above a button that opens the Space Map page. 'Space Map' is the app's interactive treemap view of disk usage.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_IncompleteScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Diese Überprüfung hat den Status {0}. Teilweise erfasste Überprüfungsdaten werden ausgeblendet; führen Sie eine neue Überprüfung vollständig aus, bevor Sie Ergebnisse, Bereinigung, Duplikate oder Speicherbelegung öffnen.</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar on the Scan Workspace page for a scan that did not finish. {0} is its state (an internal English word such as Failed or Cancelled). Explains that half-finished numbers are deliberately withheld and lists four pages of the app the user should not open until a new scan has run.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_LoadFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Der Überprüfungsbereich konnte nicht geladen werden: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar on the Scan Workspace page when opening the page threw an error. {0} is the technical error text and stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_Loaded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die Daten des Überprüfungsbereichs wurden aus einer abgeschlossenen gespeicherten Überprüfung geladen.</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page once everything has been read successfully from a finished, stored scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_Loading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Gespeicherte Überprüfungsdaten werden geladen...</value>
    <comment>[status] Information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page while the stored scan is being read from the app's database. 'persisted' means saved from an earlier run. Ends with three plain full stops in the English original.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_NoCompletedScans" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Es sind keine abgeschlossenen Überprüfungen verfügbar.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Shown as both the subtitle and the information bar on the Scan Workspace page when the app holds no finished scan at all.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_ScannerReport" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scanner-Bericht: {0}</value>
    <comment>[status] Appended to Workspace_Status_IncompleteScan, after a space, when the scanner recorded why it stopped. {0} is the scanner's own message and stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_SelectScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wählen Sie eine abgeschlossene Überprüfung aus.</value>
    <comment>[status] Text of the information bar at the bottom of the Scan Workspace page before any scan is loaded. Imperative.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Status_SessionUnavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Die angeforderte Überprüfungssitzung ist nicht verfügbar.</value>
    <comment>[status] Shown as both the subtitle and the information bar on the Scan Workspace page when the scan the user navigated to no longer exists. 'session' means one scan run.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_Loading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfungssitzung wird geladen...</value>
    <comment>[status] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading while the scan record is being read. 'session' means one scan run. Ends with three plain full stops in the English original.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_NoScan" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keine Überprüfung ausgewählt.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading before any scan has been chosen.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Summary_StatusStarted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} · gestartet am {1}</value>
    <comment>[status] Subtitle under the Scan Workspace heading once a scan is loaded. {0} is the scan's state (an internal English word such as Completed or Failed, not translated), {1} the local date and time the scan began, already formatted. The separator is a middle dot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Delta" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Delta</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page about what changed between two comparable scans of the same folder.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Errors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fehler</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing paths the scanner could not read. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dateien</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing the scan's largest individual files. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Folders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ordner</value>
    <comment>[header] Tab of the Scan Workspace page listing the scan's largest folders. Plural noun.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Tab_Overview" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Übersicht</value>
    <comment>[header] First tab of the Scan Workspace page, holding the file-type breakdown and the review queue.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfungsbereich</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the Scan Workspace page while no particular scan is loaded. The Scan Workspace gathers one scan's overview, files, folders, duplicates and errors on a single page.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Workspace_Title_ForRoot" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Überprüfung: {0}</value>
    <comment>[title] Heading of the Scan Workspace page once a scan is loaded. {0} is the folder or drive path that was scanned.</comment>
  </data>
</root>
